# Build-context hygiene. Without this, `docker build` ships ~1.35 GB to
# package a 1.9 MB corpus: 936 MB of node_modules, a 244 MB host .venv built
# for macOS, and a 96 MB local ledger. Everything excluded here is either
# rebuilt inside the image, machine-local, or a secret.

# Version control and tooling
.git
.github
.gitignore
.claude
.agents
.impeccable
.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[co]

# Host-built dependency trees — wrong platform for the image, and huge
.venv
**/node_modules
dashboard/dist

# Secrets. .env.example is the template that ships; .env never does.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Runtime state. The ledger is rebuilt from the corpus on first boot (0.3s),
# uploads and drafts belong to whoever runs the container, and the reseed
# backup is a local artifact that isn't even tracked by git.
data/ledger.db
data/sandbox.db
data/*.jsonl
data/uploads
registry/drafts

# Docs and tests aren't needed to run the service
docs
eval
tests
